            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ashley"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is delicious! I decided to bake instead of broil - 375 degrees for 30-40 minutes worked well. I doubled the sauce recipe and it gave it a good amount of flavor. I also made cuts into the Salmon so that the sauce/ glaze could flavor the inside of the meat. I served it with Jasmine rice &amp; mixed vegetables and it was a delicious meal!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Chris"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Use honey instead of brown sugar, add some soy sauce, use dry prepared mustard and you have the exact recipe that Windsor Court Grill Room uses for their Honey Mustard Glazed Salmon",
            "datePublished": "2009-06-05T03:35:02.527Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Constance Moenart"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved it! Only used 2 filets, since there are only 2 of us. The rest of the ingredients stayed the same. I did change the cooking method though. Cooked in oven at 375 degrees for 15 minutes, refreshed the glaze, then broiled for 5 minutes. Will definitely be making again.",
            "datePublished": "2022-10-08T22:22:16.113Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Natnat13"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Omg this was amazing!! The first time I made this, I followed the recipe with the broiling and it wasn’t that great. Months later, the second time, I followed the top reviewer’s suggestions of doubling the sauce, making cuts in the salmon, and baking in the oven at 375 F. Mine was done in 20 minutes and it was some of the best salmon I’ve had in my life!! Hard to believe something so simple could be so good! My dad had a bite and also said it was excellent.",
            "datePublished": "2026-06-30T22:24:21.805Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Vik L"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved it. But I'm pretty much \"one step cook\". I mixed, melter butter, mayo ( I love sir Kent, because there's no additives) , parmezhan and mazarrlla cheese, pepper poored it all over, and baked at 400 until flaky with cheese golden on top. Perfect, jucy, mild taste and melts in your mouth. I had halibut steaks 1 inch thick, baked in glass pan.",
            "datePublished": "2020-03-29T16:06:22.913Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Grace Hill"
            },
            "reviewBody": "OH MY!! I made this recipe last night. Unbelievably good. I will definitely make this recipe at least twice a month. Has plenty of possibilities by changing the dry spices. And, since my husband and I like more savory than sweet dishes, I reduced the sugar to 1 Tbs. packed brown sugar and added 1/2 tsp. garlic powder and 1/4 tsp. onion powder, 1/2 tsp. black pepper and 1/4 tsp. sea salt to the mixture. I then stirred everything in a small bowl and basted the salmon steaks (two, each about 6 oz.) on all sides, placed on a rack inside a small baking dish and broiled for 15 minutes. I did reserve about a tablespoon of the basting mixture for serving. A definite keeper. Thank you Tamara.",
            "datePublished": "2019-01-21T19:55:28.570Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Amy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is AMAZING! I mean even the kids can’t get enough of it. I have followed some of the changes in the comments to enhance the recipe though. I heat the oven to 375 and cook it for 30-40 mins. I also read the last time I made it to add small cuts in the salmon and make sure the brown sugar and mustard goes in there and it was one of the tastiest things I’ve eaten! I sometimes also add a little more brown sugar so it stays on the salmon when cooking.",
            "datePublished": "2019-02-25T21:20:33.290Z"
          },
          {
